# Cells synthesis may not use (SYNTH_EXCLUDED_CELL_FILE in config.json).
#
# This is the PDK's list (sky130A/libs.tech/openlane/sky130_fd_sc_hd/no_synth.cells, in the
# version LibreLane 3.0.14 pins) without its 116 plain drive-strength-1 cells: the logic gates,
# flip-flops, latches, adders and inverters such as nand2_1, a21o_1 and dfxtp_1. Synthesis may
# use those here; the clock, delay, scan, low-power and other special _1 cells stay excluded.
#
# The PDK left them out because their small pins can be hard for the router to reach
# (OpenLane discussion #2179), not because of a fault in the cells; cells with layout problems
# are in its separate drc_exclude.cells (PNR_EXCLUDED_CELL_FILE), which synthesis also
# honours. Upstream open_pdks has since stopped excluding the _1 cells (commit 2347071, May
# 2026). Without them every gate was a _2 cell; with them this design measured 22% less cell
# area (TT utilisation 80.5% -> 61%), with better timing, fewer slew warnings and a clean route.
#
# SPDX-FileCopyrightText: © 2026 Alexei Zverovitch
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

